  "query_preview": "..\n/Issued 1224 PM MDT Wed Sep 16 2026/ \n\n - Meteorological Overview:\n\nThe next upper level trough moves into the area out of the west on \nThursday. Due to the SW flow over central MT, there will be a \nresulting unstable airmass that develops. As such, expect rounds of \nshowers/thunderstorms to begin late Thursday morning/early afternoon \nand continue through Saturday, mainly impacting southwest/central \nMT. Additionally, there is the potential for these storms to be \nstrong.\n\nAs an upper level ridge develops over the region on Sunday, expect a \nshift towards mild and drier conditions. The ridge looks to remain \nin place through at least Monday.\n\nFor Tuesday and Wednesday, models continue to struggle on finding a \ncommon solution. - ESH\n\n - Forecast Confidence & Scenarios:\n\nThe main concern for the thunderstorms Thu night and Friday will\nbe how strong will the thunderstorms be. Some storms could produce\nstrong wind gusts and hail. Instability of CAPE could exceed 1500\nj/kg around Helena on Friday. Additionally, the airmass will \nremain unstable Thu night for thunderstorms to likely continue \nmuch of Thursday night.\n\nFor next Tue...both the GFS/EC models continue to have opposite\nsolutions, with one model warm/dry...the other model cold/wet.\nThus confidence is low at this time for next Tue. Brusda",
